.TH XUR.STD.MAP 7 "2026-11-19" "xur 0.1.3" "Xur Manual"
.SH NAME
xur.std.map \- map methods
.SH DESCRIPTION
Maps in xur are shared and change in place (like lists).
.B std::map
is not imported directly; instead these are methods on any map value
.RB ( "#{}" ).
The type is written
.B map
in annotations (e.g. a struct field or parameter); like a list, only the
container is type-checked \(em keys and values are dynamic.
.SH METHODS
.TP
.B len() -> int
Number of key-value pairs.
.TP
.B is_empty() -> bool
Whether the map has no entries.
.TP
.B get(key) -> Option<Value>
Return the value for
.IR key ,
or
.B None
if not present.
.TP
.B contains_key(key) -> bool
Whether the map contains
.IR key .
.TP
.B insert(key, value) -> ()
Insert or overwrite a key-value pair.
.TP
.B remove(key) -> Option<Value>
Remove a key and return its value, or
.B None
if not present.
.TP
.B keys() -> list
All keys as a list (unordered).
.TP
.B values() -> list
All values as a list (unordered).
.TP
.B entries() -> list
All entries as a list of (key, value) tuples.
.TP
.B clear() -> ()
Remove all entries.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
use std::io;

fn main() {
    let m = #{"a": 1, "b": 2};
    m.insert("c", 3);
    io::println("len: {}", m.len());

    match m.get("a") {
        Some(v) => io::println("a = {}", v),
        None => io::println("not found"),
    }

    for entry in m.entries() {
        io::println("{} -> {}", entry.0, entry.1);
    }
}
.fi
